    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0342" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg282"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Adee</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: During his interview with the second
                    secretary and Mr. Alexander, Waller stated that he had been subjected to cruel
                    treatment on board of the French steamer which brought him to France. He said
                    that he was chained to the floor by his arms and legs and was kept on his back
                    in that condition for seven days, and was exposed to gross indignities. As by
                    the text of your cable of the 22d instant instructions were to investigate all
                    matters connected with his trial, this statement was not included in Waller’s
                    sworn statement, but I communicate it for the information of the Department.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
